  "about": "Nine common building materials, read as the page sets them rather than reduced to a figure each: six of the nine print a density as a range, five print the modulus as a range, and every loss factor is either a range or an approximation the page marks with a tilde. The loss factor column is headed eta_int times ten to the minus three, so a printed 0.1 is a loss factor of 0.0001 and is stored as one. The modulus column is dynamic by its own footnote, except the one cell a second footnote makes static, which carries a note saying so. Glass prints a rule where its Poisson ratio would go and is served without one. The table credits no source.",
